From 8e5e1dc9f1ae4df578bf12c6141bce8cb3cbb531 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:03:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Arcane: field operations and unified memory resource

Headers compiled by the calling code with its installation of Arccore, the
core component of the Arcane framework, counterparts of the `arcane`
backend of the `generic-parallel` interface of MFront:

- `ArcaneFieldOperations` copies and fills the views with commands of
  Arccore launched on a queue (`Arcane::Accelerator::RunQueue`), on the GPU
  or on the cores of the host as selected by the queue. A copy between two
  views with the same dense layout is a copy of a contiguous memory region
  by Arccore. The ranges are split in commands of at most 2^30 points;
- `ArcaneUnifiedMemoryResource` allocates the unified memory of Arccore
  (by default), accessible by all the queues, with the over-allocation of
  the other memory resources for strict alignments. The size of the
  allocated block, required by the deallocation of Arccore, is given by
  `getOverAlignedAllocationSize`, shared with `allocateOverAligned`;
- documentation.
